---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of use" description="Terms that apply to using the GCC Enable website." updated="[Date]">
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of {site.domain}, operated by {site.legalEntity} (“GCC Enable”). By using the site you agree to
    them. Terms for training engagements are set out separately in each client agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the site</h2>
  <p>You may use this site for lawful purposes only. Do not attempt to disrupt it, gain unauthorised access or misuse the forms.</p>

  <h2>Content</h2>
  <p>
    Text, graphics, logos and materials on this site belong to GCC Enable unless stated otherwise. You may share links and short
    quotes with attribution. Please ask before reusing anything else.
  </p>

  <h2>Information only</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site is general information, not professional advice. Industry statistics are quoted from the third-party
    sources named alongside them, and we are not responsible for their accuracy.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>We link to third-party sites such as YouTube and LinkedIn. We are not responsible for their content or practices.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent permitted by law, GCC Enable is not liable for any loss arising from use of this site.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts of [Pune, Maharashtra] have jurisdiction.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
